The reaction

$$

\begin{array}{l}

2 \mathrm{Cu}^{+}(\mathrm{aq}) \longrightarrow \mathrm{Cu}(\mathrm{s})+\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(\mathrm{aq}) \\

\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{cell}}=\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{cell}}^{\circ}-\frac{0.0592}{1} \log \frac{\left[\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}\right]}{\left[\mathrm{Cu}^{+}\right]^{2}}

\end{array}

$$

At equilibrium $\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{cell}}=0$

$$

\therefore \quad \mathrm{E}_{\text {cell }}^{\circ}=0.0592 \log \mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{c}}

$$

or, $\quad \log \mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{c}}=\frac{0.52-0.16}{0.0592}$

$\therefore \mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{c}}=1.2 \times 10^{6}$

At cathodes: $\mathrm{Fe}^{+}+2 \mathrm{e}^{-} \longrightarrow \mathrm{Fe} ;$

$$

\begin{array}{l}

\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}+3 \mathrm{e}^{-} \longrightarrow \mathrm{Fe} \\

\left(\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{Fe}}\right)_{1}=\frac{\text { At. wt. }}{2} ;\left(\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{Fe}}\right)_{2}=\frac{\text { At. wt. }}{3}

\end{array}

$$

Hence, $\frac{\left(\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{Fe}}\right)_{1}}{\left(\mathrm{E}_{\mathrm{Fe}}\right)_{2}}=\frac{3}{2}$

Amt. deposited $=\frac{\text { E. wt } \times \text { Q }}{96500}$;
$$
107.870=\frac{107.870}{96500} \times \mathrm{Q} ; \quad \therefore \mathrm{Q}=96500 \mathrm{C}
$$

Solublity $=\frac{\text { conductivity } \times 1000}{\Lambda_{\text {eq }}}$
$$
\begin{array}{l}
=\frac{3.06 \times 10^{-6} \times 1000}{1.53}=2 \times 10^{-3} \\
K_{\text {sp }}=\mathrm{S}^{2}=4 \times 10^{-6}
\end{array}
$$
